  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://ontology.local/support#Product">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Product</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel>Product</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>A software product that customers license and raise support tickets about. The Product is what a license grants access to, what a ticket concerns, and what documentation describes. It is the join point between the commercial, support and knowledge parts of the model.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:comment>A software product that customers license and raise support tickets about. The Product is what a license grants access to, what a ticket concerns, and what documentation describes. It is the join point between the commercial, support and knowledge parts of the model.</rdfs:comment>
    <sup:domainType>Product</sup:domainType>
    <sup:status>Canonical</sup:status>
    <sup:identityRule>The licensing system product ID is authoritative. Version is not part of identity — a product and its versions are the same product. Version-specific facts would need `sup:ProductVersion`, which is not modelled (`OQ-15`).</sup:identityRule>
    <sup:sourceFile>Ontology/Entities/Product.md</sup:sourceFile>
    <skos:altLabel>SKU</skos:altLabel>
