  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>SupportEntitlement</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel>SupportEntitlement</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>The tier of support service an account is entitled to receive. The tier governs response time targets, escalation rights and channel access. Entitlement is a property of the account, not of an individual ticket or license.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:comment>The tier of support service an account is entitled to receive. The tier governs response time targets, escalation rights and channel access. Entitlement is a property of the account, not of an individual ticket or license.</rdfs:comment>
    <sup:domainType>Customer</sup:domainType>
    <sup:status>Canonical</sup:status>
    <sup:identityRule>Natural key: the canonical tier code (`STANDARD`, `PREMIUM`). Entitlement is a controlled vocabulary, not a per-account record — the per-account fact is the `hasEntitlement` link, and its effective dates live on the link.</sup:identityRule>
    <sup:sourceFile>Ontology/Entities/SupportEntitlement.md</sup:sourceFile>
